{"data":{"brief":".canon/changes/b/brief.md","changeId":"b","subjectId":"s"},"meta":{"command":"change new","next":[{"actor":"human","command":"report the pending draft's brief in .canon/changes/b/brief.md to the human; s is not blocked meanwhile","role":null,"why":"s: `b` is a pending draft (.canon/changes/b/brief.md has no `Approved:` line) and not yet part of the subject's scope: reopen, evidence and ship read the newest approved change until a scenario is tagged `@flow:b.*`, and then the subject cannot ship until the human answers; once they do, record their words with `canon brief approve --change-id b --by <the human> --note \"<their words>\"`"},{"actor":"agent","command":"canon scenario new <area>.<surface>.01 --title \"<behavior>\" --subject-id s --case happy --actor-id <unit>","role":"implementer","why":"s owns no scenario; specify its behavior, one scenario per behavior"}],"warnings":["subject `s` is building and change `b` is not approved (.canon/changes/b/brief.md has no `Approved:` line): the subject's existing scenarios keep accepting evidence, and while no scenario is tagged `@flow:b.*` it can still be reopened and shipped for its approved scope; once a scenario is tagged `@flow:b.*`, those scenarios wait for the approval and `s` cannot ship until the brief is approved; to take the adoption back run `canon subject unadopt b --subject-id s`"]}}
